  "database": "rschema_0344",
  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0344' consists of 8 tables. The 'User' table is used to store user information, including the user's email, unique identifier, and username. The 'Application' table stores information about the applications, including the application's unique identifier, code, name, and type. The 'Web_Service' table contains information about web services, including the unique identifier of the application they belong to, creation date, description, name, and the unique identifier of the service itself. The 'Permissions' table stores information about the permissions of users on different applications, including the unique identifiers of the application and user, and the role. The 'Error_Information' table stores information about errors, including the unique identifier of the error, error code, description, occurrence time, return status, and the unique identifier of the service it belongs to. The 'Service_Monitoring' table stores information about service monitoring, including the call time, delay time, unique identifier of the monitoring, return status, and the unique identifier of the service. The 'Statistics' table stores statistics about services, including the call count, success rate, time period, and the unique identifier of the service. Finally, the 'Error_and_Monitoring_Association' table is used to associate errors with their corresponding monitoring records, using the unique identifiers of the error and monitoring records. All these tables have foreign keys that reference the primary keys of other tables, ensuring referential integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nThis system is designed for managing and monitoring web services in various applications. Key requirements include:\nEach user has a unique username, email, and role. User roles are associated with specific permissions. Users can be assigned different roles and permissions that are linked to particular applications.\nEach application has a unique ID, code, name, and type.\nEach web service has a unique ID, name, description, and creation date. It records error information, including error codes, descriptions, timestamps, and return status.\nMonitors the invocation of web services, recording details like invocation time, return status, delay time, and other performance metrics.\nTracks statistics such as success rate and call count over a specific time period.\nTracks which users are authorized to access which applications.\nLinks error data with monitoring data to enable detailed analysis and reporting.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0344.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0344\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Application` (\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`application_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Web_Service` (\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`service_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `web_service_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`application_id`) REFERENCES `Application` (`application_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Permissions` (\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`application_id`) REFERENCES `Application` (`application_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Error_Information` (\n  `error_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `error_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `occurrence_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `return_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`error_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `error_information_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `Web_Service` (`service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Service_Monitoring` (\n  `monitoring_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `call_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `delay_time` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `return_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`monitoring_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `service_monitoring_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `Web_Service` (`service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Statistics` (\n  `statistics_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `call_count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `success_rate` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `time_period` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`statistics_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `statistics_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `Web_Service` (`service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Error_and_Monitoring_Association` (\n  `association_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `error_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `monitoring_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`association_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `error_and_monitoring_association_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`error_id`) REFERENCES `Error_Information` (`error_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `error_and_monitoring_association_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`monitoring_id`) REFERENCES `Service_Monitoring` (`monitoring_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
